Z||000000||rockcrawl||09-30-2000||07:33 PM||||My '87 GT is just sitting waiting for a new engine. I opened the rear hood the other day to get something out and I heard a rush of water go toward the front of the lid as I lifted it. The water trickled out a hole in the front. There was also water sitting in the trunk. Any idea how the water gets in? I don't think it comes in through the wing mounts because those holes only go through the top layer of SMC. That could be where the water gets into the trunk, but how does it get inside the hood. Anyone else have this problem? The car was parked on a slight slope toward the passenger side for at least a month.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||13
